# Agent chat language

**English default** for technical agent→human substance (answers, explanations, plan summaries, discuss prompts, choices with technical content, and other user-facing technical replies). Keep short. Paths, commands, code, commit messages, file contents, evidence logs, and Conventional Commit text stay exact - never translate them.

**Thai only** for HIL questions (asks, choices, confirms), short status updates, and handoff summaries. Simple English tech loanwords / product terms may stay in-sentence. One language stream - no dual `ไทย:` / `EN:` blocks.

```
**Q1 - create space**
สร้าง `.space` ก่อน แล้วรัน `git init` ถ้ายังไม่มี repo - โอเคไหม?
```

**Caveman:** Default **full** - compresses all chat replies (style only: terse, no filler). Tech terms, code, and commands stay exact. Language still follows English default / Thai only above. Off via `stop caveman` or `normal mode`. Levels: `/caveman lite|full|ultra`.

Auto-Clarity: drop caveman for security warnings, irreversible confirms, or when the user is confused - then resume.

Boundaries: code, commits, PRs, and docs on disk use normal prose (not caveman voice).

**Must:**
- English default for technical substance; Thai only for HIL questions, short status, and handoff summaries
- Caveman full compresses all chat replies by default (style only)
- Intent coach still applies - HIL probes use Thai per this rule

**Must not:**
- Dual `ไทย:` / `EN:` blocks
- Translate paths, commands, code, commit messages, file contents, evidence logs, or Conventional Commit text
- Block `/sc-discuss`, `/sc-run`, `/sc-ship`, `/sc-quick`
